[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    270[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    271[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **`LZ4F_*` enum-typed struct fields were signed in the Rust translation.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    272[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    273[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `LZ4F_blockSizeID_t`, `LZ4F_blockMode_t`, `LZ4F_contentChecksum_t`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    274[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `LZ4F_blockChecksum_t` and `LZ4F_frameType_t` are C enums whose enumerators are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    275[0m:[38;5;10m[49m all non-negative, so GCC gives them an **unsigned** 32-bit underlying type
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    276[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (confirmed empirically: `(LZ4F_contentChecksum_t)-1 < 0` is false, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    277[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `(size_t)(LZ4F_contentChecksum_t)-1 == 4294967295`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    278[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    279[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/src/lz4frame.rs` declared the corresponding `LZ4F_frameInfo_t`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    280[0m:[38;5;10m[49m fields as `c_int` and widened them with `as usize`, which **sign-extends**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    281[0m:[38;5;10m[49m With `contentChecksumFlag = i32::MIN`, `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` therefore
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    282[0m:[38;5;10m[49m returned `0xFFFFFFFE_00007563` in Rust versus `0x00000002_00007563` in C — a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    283[0m:[38;5;10m[49m difference of 2^34 in the reported bound. The same signedness also changed the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    284[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `while (requestedBSID > proposedBSID)` loop in `LZ4F_optimalBSID` for negative
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    285[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `blockSizeID` values.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    286[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    287[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Fix: the five enum-typed fields, the matching constants, `LZ4F_getBlockSize`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    288[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `LZ4F_optimalBSID`, `LZ4F_initStream_internal`, `LZ4F_selectCompression` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    289[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `LZ4F_makeBlock`'s `crcFlag` now use `c_uint`, matching the C ABI. Caught by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    290[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/lz4frame_errors.rs::e157_out_of_range_enums`.
